<bioghist encodinganalog="545$a">
<head>Biographical/Historical Information
</head>
<p>Ralph S. Northam was elected 73rd governor of the Commonwealth of Virginia on 7 November 2017 and inaugurated on 13 January 2018. He served until 15 January 2022.</p>
</bioghist>
<scopecontent encodinganalog="520$a">
<head>Scope and Content
</head>
<p>Correspondence, 2018-2021, from constituents of Governor Ralph S. Northam, including requests for assistance and inquiries about the Governor's stance on certain policy issues. Also included are letters from federal and state agencies, local government officials, Virginia General Assembly members, members of the U.S. Congress, and others, including the U.S. President, governors of other states and ambassadors. The Northam administration was dominated by issues: Covid, Climate, Mountain Valley and Atlantic Coast Pipelines, and a call for his resignation.</p>
</scopecontent>
<arrangement encodinganalog="351">
<head>Arrangement
</head>
<p>This collection is arranged chronologically, with mass mailings located at the end.</p>
</arrangement>
